 ],
 "reading": "The re-entry rule, not the threshold, decides the result. Fixed-N re-entry walks back into 2000-02 and 2008. SMA200 re-entry at 8-12% is one plateau: CAGR 9.4-10.7% vs hold 10.8%, worst fall -27 to -34% vs -55%. It costs ~3.6 pts/yr in the 2010-26 bull half and earns ~3 pts/yr in 1993-2009. 5%+SMA has the best ratio but fires 94 times: the fitted cell, not the rule. Firm decision: keep the pre-registered 10%; add the mechanical re-entry (SPY > SMA200 and >=21 sessions) as v3 for prereg-reviewer. The threshold was chosen, not fitted; a 3% stop is ruled out (CAGR 3.4% at N21, 6.1% at BOTH21).",
 "source_note": "Copied from the estate's research record of 2026-10-22; only this `data` line was generalised (it named a private path). Reproduced from a fresh yfinance download on 2026-10-24: results/stop_rule_grid_yfinance_2026-10-24.json (python -m riskgate grid --download SPY --end 2026-10-17 --compare results/stop_rule_grid.json)."
